The `useState` initializer captures `encryptedAuthToken` at component mount, but this value comes from `useSession()` and could change if the session updates. Since the initializer only runs once, the `sourceURL` will never reflect session changes.

**Fix**: Derive `sourceURL` directly in the component body instead of using `useState`:
```tsx
// Remove useState, derive directly
const sourceURL = useMemo(
  () => VideoUtils.addSkipTimeTagToURL(
    url.includes('blob:') || url.includes('file:///') 
      ? url 
      : addEncryptedAuthTokenToURL(url, encryptedAuthToken), 
    0.001
  ),
  [url, encryptedAuthToken]
);
```

