The `optimisticWaiting` state is cleared via useEffect when `serverLabel` arrives. This is unnecessary state synchronization - the condition can be computed directly without state updates.

**Fix**: Derive the processing state directly:

```typescript
// Remove this useEffect entirely
// useEffect(() => {
//     if (\!serverLabel || \!optimisticWaiting) {
//         return;
//     }
//     setOptimisticWaiting(false);
// }, [serverLabel, optimisticWaiting]);

// Instead, compute isProcessing directly:
const isProcessing = isConciergeChat && (\!\!serverLabel || (optimisticWaiting && \!serverLabel));

// Or simplify the kickoffWaitingIndicator to set a timestamp:
const [optimisticStartTime, setOptimisticStartTime] = useState<number | null>(null);

const kickoffWaitingIndicator = useCallback(() => {
    if (\!isConciergeChat || serverLabel) {
        return;
    }
    setOptimisticStartTime(Date.now());
}, [isConciergeChat, serverLabel]);

// Then derive:
const isProcessing = isConciergeChat && (\!\!serverLabel || \!\!optimisticStartTime);
```

