The dependency array includes the entire `policy` object, which will cause the callback to be recreated whenever any property of the policy changes, even if `policy.id` (the only value used) remains the same. This causes unnecessary re-renders.

**Suggested fix:**
Since `policyID` is already derived from `policy` earlier in the component (line 97: `const policyID = policy?.id;`), use `policyID` in the dependency array instead of `policy`:

```tsx
const handleLeaveWorkspace = useCallback(() => {
    if (!policy) {
        return;
    }

    leaveWorkspace(policy);
    setIsLeaveModalOpen(false);
    goBackFromInvalidPolicy();
}, [policy, goBackFromInvalidPolicy]); // Add goBackFromInvalidPolicy to dependencies
```

Or better yet, since `policyID` is already derived:
```tsx
const handleLeaveWorkspace = useCallback(() => {
    if (!policyID) {
        return;
    }

    leaveWorkspace(policy);
    setIsLeaveModalOpen(false);
    goBackFromInvalidPolicy();
}, [policyID, policy, goBackFromInvalidPolicy]); // Use policyID for stability
```

