The `useEffect` triggers on every `text` change, but the telemetry span should only be ended once when this specific message is first rendered. Running `Performance.markEnd` and `endSpan` on every text change is inefficient and could produce incorrect telemetry data.

Since the goal is to measure the time from sending a message until it appears on screen, the effect should only run once when the component with the matching `reportActionID` first mounts:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
    if (reportActionID) {
        Performance.markEnd(CONST.TIMING.SEND_MESSAGE, {message: text});
        endSpan(`${CONST.TELEMETRY.SPAN_SEND_MESSAGE}_${reportActionID}`);
    }
    // Only run once on mount - not on text changes
    // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
}, [reportActionID]);
```

This ensures the measurement only happens once per message, not on every re-render.

